From 48aa08585dc055fd750377985f6c19eee521c6e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shyalya <shyalya@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 11:25:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] A seated trainer could not teach anything

Delarion Featherwing, the herbalist in Alah'Thalas, would not train herbalism.
Clicking Train did nothing at all: no message, no money taken, nothing in the
log. His npc_trainer rows are identical to those of a trainer that works, the
learn spell and its skill line are intact, and the gossip route to the trainer
list is correct.

The learning spell is not cast by the player but by the trainer, and CheckCast
rejects any caster that is not standing up. He sits at his table - creature_addon
stand_state = 1 - so every purchase came back SPELL_FAILED_NOT_STANDING. The
handler then sends TRAIN_FAIL_UNAVAILABLE, which the client does not display,
which is why this looked like nothing happening at all rather than a failure.

He is currently the only seated trainer on the realm, so this could have been a
one-row data change. It belongs here instead: sitting is what the NPC was built
to do, and the next trainer placed at a table would hit the same wall.

Only seated trainers are affected - they now cast the learning spell as
triggered. Everything that check would otherwise catch has already been verified
by this point: interaction, line of sight, that the spell is on this trainer's
list, that the player can learn it, and that they can afford it.

Found through the error line added earlier in this handler, which reported cast
result 62 against creature 61842.
---
 src/game/Handlers/NPCHandler.cpp | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/game/Handlers/NPCHandler.cpp b/src/game/Handlers/NPCHandler.cpp
index a498bdd..c5be4f3 100644
--- a/src/game/Handlers/NPCHandler.cpp
+++ b/src/game/Handlers/NPCHandler.cpp
@@ -337,11 +337,21 @@ void WorldSession::HandleTrainerBuySpellOpcode(WorldPacket & recv_data)
     _player->RemoveAurasWithInterruptFlags(AURA_INTERRUPT_FLAG_TALK);
     _player->RemoveSpellsCausingAura(SPELL_AURA_MOUNTED);
 
+    // A seated trainer cannot teach. The learning spell is cast by the trainer,
+    // and CheckCast refuses any caster that is not standing up, so the purchase
+    // failed with SPELL_FAILED_NOT_STANDING - silently, since the client shows
+    // nothing for TRAIN_FAIL_UNAVAILABLE and no money changes hands. Turtle has
+    // trainers who sit at their tables by design, so rather than stand them up,
+    // let them cast this as triggered. Everything that check would otherwise
+    // catch has already been verified above: interaction, line of sight, that
+    // the spell is on this trainer's list, that it can be learned, and money.
+    bool const seatedTrainer = !unit->IsStandingUp();
+
     Spell *spell;
     if (proto->SpellVisual == 222)
         spell = new Spell(_player, proto, false);
     else
-        spell = new Spell(unit, proto, false);
+        spell = new Spell(unit, proto, seatedTrainer);
 
     SpellCastTargets targets;
     targets.setUnitTarget(_player);
